an annual event held by the UN nuclear  Watchdog at its headquarters  this year over 2 500 participants from  175 member states director General  Rafael Grossi opened the session  highlighting the organization's main  objective to maintain nuclear safety  across the world  now more critical than ever given  historic events such as Russia's  invasion of Ukraine is the root cause  and that led to this heated debate on  Thursday when Canada and Poland  spearheaded a joint statement on behalf  of 50 delegates in which they call on  the Russian Federation to seize all  activities at the Zappa region nuclear  power plant immediately  the iea's latest report on safety  concerns around the zapparesia nuclear  plant delivered in September raised  serious concerns about a possible  nuclear disaster if the military  activities continue around the plant  the agency has passed two resolutions  this year calling on all parties to  cease military activities near the plant  Russia's ambassador to the agency  insists his country has no military  Presence at the plant but rather  National Guards and blamed Ukraine for  continuing to attack Europe's largest  nuclear power plant Ambassador Mikhail  ulyanov also called Ukraine's proposal  for a demilitarized zone around the  plant an unrealistic demand  I will not comment on the speech of the  representative of Russia I will only say  that everything he said is a complete  lie Iran's nuclear program was in the  spotlight as the head of Iran's atomic  energy agency delivered the opening  speech at the conference Muhammad islami  stressed the need for sanctions relief  before return to the 2015 nuclear deal  which saw Tehran limit its nuclear  program  islami held two rounds of talks with  director General Grossi privately on the  sidelines at the conference the first  such meetings between the two men since  June  iaea's latest report on Iran indicates  the agency is no longer able to provide  reassurances that Iran's nuclear program  is entirely peaceful  as a conference draws to a close a  number of resolutions have passed one  urging the Democratic People's Republic  of Korea to abide by the safeguards of  the non-proliferation treaty another one  on nuclear safety in the Middle East  calling on all those countries to extend  their full cooperation to the director  General so he can do his job which is to  ensure non-proliferation whether These  Warnings will have the desired outcome  remains to be seen  dorsa chapari Al Jazeera Vienna
 

